**Theorem 4.2 (row correspondence and completed-predecessor closure).**
On the canonical initialized instance of Theorem 2.5,
$\operatorname{Step}_{\rm sel}$ reproduces each actual row, receipt,
event and successor with its authentic input. At every reached $R_r$ with
authentic finite completed $M$, Boundary returns its exact $a,b$ in finite
paid work, and Prefix for $a\le k\le b$ returns precisely that same run's
length-$k$ prefix and raw endpoint. The assertion includes earlier
executions of this selector, their interpreters and every partial phase
of their native expansion.

Proof. ARC Proposition 6.3/RCA Proposition 12.5 supplies the ten local
cases. The added rows still have precisely those cases: mode IN changes
one ingress latch; EX, WR and moves have their actual single-cell effects;
its tests and handoffs name fixed finite CTL/TOK slots. Parser, arithmetic,
list and binding operations are expanded rows, not new local effects.
Using the actual finite table and Definition 3.3's additional IN site
therefore gives the same proof at each added row. In particular the mode
IN-before-WR successor has its new latch and old70 destination, and an EX
successor has the actual blank before WR. All partial bank/control/
descriptor/copy rows keep their full physical projection.

For completion use simultaneous induction on completed outer cycles, as
in ARC Proposition 6.5 and RCA Lemma 15.1. Zero cycles have Theorem 2.5's
finite activation prefix. An auxiliary cycle has CAP Lemma 6.7's finite
original source/row/ACK return, followed by the explicit normalization
and CaptureCAP. A history cycle freezes a strictly shorter completed
predecessor. By induction Boundary follows its already finite actual
prefix; §§5–6 below use only finite acquired words, bounded replay and
finite channel loops. They therefore finish and append the next cycle.
Simulating a row that happens to lie inside an earlier interpreter still
executes one literal RD/WR/etc. It does not recursively ask for the semantic
result of that earlier Call. Each Step's finite table/cell scans terminate.
The induction is on completed predecessors, not the size or future outcome
of the currently executing simulation.

The Boundary conjunction is false at preactivation entries and earlier
Readies with smaller counts; following the exact prefix reaches the
intended one. Its tally is consequently $b$. Prefix's $k$ decreasing marks
give exactly $k$ represented rows and the authentic $I_k$, including a
last input bit still in its latch. No reservoir suffix affects a prefix
before its next IN. This proves the claimed finite correspondence under
the stated actual-supply/local-completion premises; it supplies no live
permission at the represented old endpoint. ∎

